\begin{equation}
  \hat{R}^{(m)}_u=\frac{1}{M}\sum_{i=1}^{M}\!\textit{success}^{(m)}(u,K_i),
\end{equation}
where $K_i$ are i.i.d.\ failure sets at fraction $p_{\mathrm{fail}}$.
Each trial removes failed services (and, under async semantics, Kafka edges) and checks reachability on the remaining graph.
We use $M=5\times 10^{6}$ trials per job; the resulting Monte Carlo noise is negligible after averaging over repeated jobs.
